        "original_id": "ce0cf949-2511-574a-9f2c-0864854356c9",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Lewis Terman, G. Stanley Hall\n- Projects: Genetic Studies of Genius\n- Organizations: Stanford University\n- Topics: psychology, gifted children, citation rankings\n\nFacts:\n- G. Stanley Hall was a pioneering American psychologist and educator who lived from February 1, 1846, to April 24, 1924.\n- Lewis Terman was an American psychologist and author who lived from January 15, 1877, to December 21, 1956.\n- Lewis Terman began the Genetic Studies of Genius at Stanford University in 1921 to examine the development and characteristics of gifted children into adulthood.\n- A Review of General Psychology survey published in 2002 ranked Lewis Terman as the 72nd most cited psychologist of the 20th century, tied with G. Stanley Hall.",
